%description:

A deviation of the BLER lookup from the table it reads, recorded rather than
fixed: GetBLER_TU (BLERvsSINR_15CQI_TU.h) does not return the tabulated BLER at
the two ends of a curve.

The curves are measured points, and the table is the only oracle there is: at
a tabulated SINR, the lookup ought to give the tabulated BLER. At the ends it
does not, because the saturation branches take over at the end points
themselves:

 - SINR <= the first point gives 1.0, whatever the table says there. CQI 14
   and 15 tabulate 0.98 and 0.964 at their first points.
 - SINR >= the last point gives 0.0, and the last column of BLER_15_CQI_TU is
   never read. CQI 11-15 tabulate an error floor there (0.02, 0.008, 0.02,
   0.004, 0.02), so the lookup falls from the interpolated value to 0 at the
   last point: a cliff, and an optimistic one.

Whether the table's floor should continue beyond its last point is a
modelling question; that the lookup reproduces the table at the table's own
points is not. BlerCqiRoundTrip pins what the lookup does today, so that any
change to it fails there by name; when the lookup honours the end points,
update those pins and drop the %expected-failure line here.

%expected-failure: the BLER lookup saturates at the curves' end points instead of returning the tabulated BLER there

%includes:
#include <string>
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "simu5g/common/blerCurves/BLERvsSINR_15CQI_TU.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;

%activity:
Checker c;

std::string firstDetail, lastDetail;
bool firstOk = true, lastOk = true;
for (int cqi = 1; cqi <= 15; cqi++) {
    int row = cqi - 1;
    double atFirst = GetBLER_TU(SINR_15_CQI_TU[row][0], cqi);
    double atLast = GetBLER_TU(SINR_15_CQI_TU[row][15], cqi);
    if (atFirst != BLER_15_CQI_TU[row][0]) {
        firstOk = false;
        firstDetail += " cqi" + std::to_string(cqi) + ": " + std::to_string(atFirst) + " (table "
                + std::to_string(BLER_15_CQI_TU[row][0]) + ")";
    }
    if (atLast != BLER_15_CQI_TU[row][15]) {
        lastOk = false;
        lastDetail += " cqi" + std::to_string(cqi) + ": " + std::to_string(atLast) + " (table "
                + std::to_string(BLER_15_CQI_TU[row][15]) + ")";
    }
}
c.check("at each curve's first tabulated SINR the lookup gives the tabulated BLER", firstOk, firstDetail);
c.check("at each curve's last tabulated SINR the lookup gives the tabulated BLER", lastOk, lastDetail);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=2 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
